{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And all Naphtali.</b> He showed him its land in its tranquility and in its destruction, and He showed him Deborah and Barak from Kedesh Naphtali warring against Sisera and his hosts." "<b>And the land of Ephraim and Manasseh.</b> He showed him their land in its tranquility and in its destruction, and He showed him Joshua warring against the kings of Canaan who came from Ephraim, and Gideon who came from Manasseh warring against Midian and Amalek." "<b>And all the land of Judah.</b> In its tranquility and in its destruction, and He showed him the kingdom of the house of David and their victories." "<b>Until the sea of the Negev.</b> The land of the west in its tranquility and in its destruction; another interpretation — do not read הַיָּם הָאַחֲרוֹן but הַיּוֹם הָאַחֲרוֹן: the Holy One, blessed be He, showed him all the events that are destined to befall Israel until the dead live (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {3 "Rashi's lemma follows the verse text עד הים האחרון; I rendered the lemma literally as written, and in the body preserved Rashi's own play on ים/יום (sea/day) by transliterating both Hebrew forms rather than translating."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:58.900097233Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}